my/question-capture-workers/linear/14038863/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-174447" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The intersection of a family of indexed sets ${{A}_{i}}_{i\\in I}$ contains all elements that belong to *all* sets in our family:\n\n$$\n{⋂}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}={x\\in U\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{i}\\,\\,\\text{for all }{A}_{i},\\,\\,i\\in I}\n$$\n\nwhere $U$ is a universal set.\n\nLet's now write down a few instances of our indexed sets:\n\n- if $i=-1,$ we have ${X}_{-1}={-2,-1}$\n\n- if $i=0,$ we have ${X}_{0}={-1,0}$\n\n- if $i=1,$ we have ${X}_{1}={0,1}$\n\nand so on. \n\nNotice that there is no element that belongs to all the sets. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{⋂}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}=∅.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038863/state.json" "file_sha256" "6450dd7505d899bc08eefb0d4bdb0216ac4dcc1cfb5eaba8bef3922f75b5e157" "basis" 1346 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038863/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-174447" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038863/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "738a4e0cbcad33d280093808d8491a29f9b6bae5ddd19b897166250d0475262a" "basis" 1346 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038863/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-174447" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038863/state.json" "file_sha256" "6450dd7505d899bc08eefb0d4bdb0216ac4dcc1cfb5eaba8bef3922f75b5e157" "basis" 1346 "verifica