nce/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038863/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-174447" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "∅"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038863/state.json" "file_sha256" "6450dd7505d899bc08eefb0d4bdb0216ac4dcc1cfb5eaba8bef3922f75b5e157" "basis" 1346 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038863/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-12665" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $T_2$ given that $T_n = \\{ 1, 2, \\ldots, 2n+1 \\},$ where $n \\in \\mathbb{N}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038863/example-12665.json" "file_sha256" "d2fd96dc6549b476e8994e34d258b81f19a901dacd61bfbb3b4ebec69783e58a" "basis" 1346 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038863/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-12665" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To write down the elements of $T_2,$ we substitute $n=2$ into the expression and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{2} & ={1,2,…,2(2)+1} \\\\  & ={1,2,…,5} \\\\  & ={1,2,3,4,5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038863/example-12665.json" "file_sha256" "d2fd96dc6549b476e8994e34d258b81f19a901dacd61bfbb3b4ebec69783e58a" "basis" 1346 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038863/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-12763" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $\\,\\displaystyle \\bigcup_{i \\in I} S_i$, given that $I = \\{ -1, 0, 1 \\},$ and $S_i = (i-1, \\,i+1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038863/example-12763.json" "file_sha256" "62092102364635426c4b4d071229d0bdfe10c6585943fb6d6896f448c2c06cbc" "basis" 1346 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038863/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-12763" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The union of a family of indexed sets is the set containing all elements belonging to *at least one* set in the indexed family:\n\n$$\n\\bigcup_{i \\in I} A_i = \\big\\{ x\\in U \\: : \\: x \\in A_i \\:\\:\\textrm{for at least one } A_i,\\:\\: i \\in I \\big\\}\n$$\n\nwhere $U$ is a universal set.\n\nTherefore, in our case, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{⋃}_{i\\in I}{S}_{i} & ={S}_{-1}\\cup {S}_{0}\\cup {S}_{1} \\\\  & =(-2,0)\\,\\cup \\,(-1,1)\\,\\cup \\,(0,2) \\\\  & =(-2,2).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038863/example-12763.json" "file_sha256" "62092102364635426c4b4d071229d0bdfe10c6585943fb6d6896f448c2c06cbc" "basis" 1346 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038863/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-12764" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $\\,\\displaystyle \\bigcap_{i \\in I} X_i$  given that $I = \\mathbb{N}$ and $X_i = \\{ i, \\, 2i \\}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038863/example-12764.json" "file_sha256" "8b35ed7e77dc4a3d2115c084f8b2afb401f7a412bfda70b050d4a109157f0f51" "basis" 1346 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038863/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-12764" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The intersection of a family of indexed sets $\\{A_i\\}_{i\\in I}$ contains all elements that belong to *all* sets in our family:\n\n$$\n\\bigcap_{i \\in I} A_i = \\big\\{ x\\in U \\: : \\: x \\in A_i \\:\\:\\textrm{for all } A_i,\\:\\: i \\in I \\big\\}\n$$\n\nwhere $U$ is a universal set.\n\nLet's now write down a few instances of our indexed sets:\n\n- if $i=1,$ we have $X_1 = \\{ 1, 2 \\}$\n\n- if $i=2,$ we have $X_2 = \\{ 2, 4 \\}$\n\n- if $i=3,$ we have $X_3 = \\{ 3, 6 \\}$\n\n- if $i=4,$ we have $X_4 = \\{ 4, 8 \\}$\n\nand so on. \n\nNotice that there is no element that belongs to all the sets. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{⋂}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}=∅.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038863/example-12764.json" "file_sha256" "8b35ed7e77dc4a3d2115c084f8b2afb401f7a412bfda70b050d4a109157f0f51" "basis" 1346 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038863/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-172662" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let ${A}_{i}={-{i}^{2},0,2i},$ where $i\\in {1,2,3,4,5}.$ Then, ${A}_{2}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071758/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b8d3481284f189b1c8e9a41b8d7e2aaa0114ab8d11d76052c51cb913db60674"} {"question" "q-172662" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To write down the elements of ${A}_{2},$ we substitute $i=2$ into the expression and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & ={-(2)^{2},\\,0,\\,2(2)} \\\\  & ={-4,0,4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071758/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b8d3481284f189b1c8e9a41b8d7e2aaa0114ab8d11d76052c51cb913db60674"} {"question" "q-172662" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficult