x\\in {A}_{i}\\,\\,\\text{for at least one }{A}_{i},\\,\\,i\\in I}\n$$\n\nwhere $U$ is a universal set.\n\nLet's now write down a few instances of our indexed sets:\n\n- if $i=1,$ we have ${S}_{1}=[1,2]$\n\n- if $i=2,$ we have ${S}_{2}=[2,5]$\n\n- if $i=3,$ we have ${S}_{3}=[3,10]$\n\nand so on.\n\nNotice that as $i$ increases the left and right endpoints of the intervals approaches $\\infty .$ The smallest left endpoint is $1.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{⋃}_{i\\in I}{S}_{i}=[1,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071758/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b8d3481284f189b1c8e9a41b8d7e2aaa0114ab8d11d76052c51cb913db60674"} {"question" "q-174454" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071758/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "329b3f8b9e5ae2380f658ef1537c5a4febf7c7d1c95f0606f2882845984220fa"} {"question" "q-174454" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071758/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b8d3481284f189b1c8e9a41b8d7e2aaa0114ab8d11d76052c51cb913db60674"} {"question" "q-174454" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[1,2]"] ["math" "[1,3]"] ["math" "[1,\\infty )"] ["math" "[2,\\infty )"] ["math" "∅"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071758/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b8d3481284f189b1c8e9a41b8d7e2aaa0114ab8d11d76052c51cb913db60674"} {"question" "q-174454" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[1,\\infty )"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071758/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b8d3481284f189b1c8e9a41b8d7e2aaa0114ab8d11d76052c51cb913db60674"} {"question" "q-174450" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $I=N$ and ${X}_{i}={-i,\\,0,\\,i},$ then ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071758/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b8d3481284f189b1c8e9a41b8d7e2aaa0114ab8d11d76052c51cb913db60674"} {"question" "q-174450" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The union of a family of indexed sets is the set containing all elements belonging to *at least one* set in the indexed family:\n\n$$\n{⋃}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}={x\\in U\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{i}\\,\\,\\text{for at least one }{A}_{i},\\,\\,i\\in I}\n$$\n\nwhere $U$ is a universal set.\n\nLet's now write down a few instances of our indexed sets:\n\n- if $i=1,$ we have ${X}_{1}={-1,0,1}$\n\n- if $i=2,$ we have ${X}_{2}={-2,0,2}$\n\n- if $i=3,$ we have ${X}_{3}={-3,0,3}$\n\nand so on. \n\nNotice that all the integers belong to one of the sets.\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}=Z.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071758/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b8d3481284f189b1c8e9a41b8d7e2aaa0114ab8d11d76052c51cb913db60674"} {"question" "q-174450" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071758/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "329b3f8b9e5ae2380f658ef1537c5a4febf7c7d1c95f0606f2882845984220fa"} {"question" "q-174450" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071758/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b8d3481284f189b1c8e9a41b8d7e2aaa0114a