$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071758/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b8d3481284f189b1c8e9a41b8d7e2aaa0114ab8d11d76052c51cb913db60674"} {"question" "q-174452" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071758/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "329b3f8b9e5ae2380f658ef1537c5a4febf7c7d1c95f0606f2882845984220fa"} {"question" "q-174452" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071758/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b8d3481284f189b1c8e9a41b8d7e2aaa0114ab8d11d76052c51cb913db60674"} {"question" "q-174452" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[0,1)"] ["math" "[0,1]"] ["math" "[0,2]"] ["math" "[0,3)"] ["math" "[1,2]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071758/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b8d3481284f189b1c8e9a41b8d7e2aaa0114ab8d11d76052c51cb913db60674"} {"question" "q-174452" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[0,2]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071758/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b8d3481284f189b1c8e9a41b8d7e2aaa0114ab8d11d76052c51cb913db60674"} {"question" "q-174447" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $I=Z$ and ${X}_{i}={i-1,\\,i},$ then ${⋂}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071758/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b8d3481284f189b1c8e9a41b8d7e2aaa0114ab8d11d76052c51cb913db60674"} {"question" "q-174447" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The intersection of a family of indexed sets ${{A}_{i}}_{i\\in I}$ contains all elements that belong to *all* sets in our family:\n\n$$\n{⋂}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}={x\\in U\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{i}\\,\\,\\text{for all }{A}_{i},\\,\\,i\\in I}\n$$\n\nwhere $U$ is a universal set.\n\nLet's now write down a few instances of our indexed sets:\n\n- if $i=-1,$ we have ${X}_{-1}={-2,-1}$\n\n- if $i=0,$ we have ${X}_{0}={-1,0}$\n\n- if $i=1,$ we have ${X}_{1}={0,1}$\n\nand so on. \n\nNotice that there is no element that belongs to all the sets. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{⋂}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}=∅.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071758/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b8d3481284f189b1c8e9a41b8d7e2aaa0114ab8d11d76052c51cb913db60674"} {"question" "q-174447" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071758/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "329b3f8b9e5ae2380f658ef1537c5a4febf7c7d1c95f0606f2882845984220fa"} {"question" "q-174447" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071758/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b8d3481284f189b1c8e9a41b8d7e2aaa0114ab8d11d76052c51cb913db60674"} {"question" "q-174447" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "Z"] ["math" "{0,\\,1}"] ["math" "{0}"] ["math" "{i}"] ["math" "∅"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071758/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b8d3481284f189b1c8e9a41b8d7e2aaa0114ab8d11d76052c51cb913db60674"} {"question" "q-174447" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "∅"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071758/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b8d3481284f189b1c8e9a41b8d7e2aaa0114ab8d11d76052c51cb913db60674"} {"question" "q-174449" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $I=N$ and ${X}_{i}={0,2,…,2i},$ then ${⋂}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071758/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b8d3481284f189b1c8e9a41b8d7e2aaa0114ab8d11d76052c51cb913db60674"} {"question" "q-174449" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The intersection of a family of indexed sets ${{A}_{i}}_{i\\in I}$ contains all elements that belong to *all* sets in our family:\n\n$$\n{⋂}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}={x\\in U\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{i}\\,\\,\\text{for all }{A}_{i},\\,\\,i\\in I}\n$$\n\nwhere $U$ is a universal set.\n\nLet's now write down a few instances of our indexed sets:\n\n- if $i=1,$ we have ${X}_{1}={0,2}$\n\n- if $i=2,$ we have ${X}_{2}={0,2,4}$\n\n- if $i=3,$ we have ${X}_{3}={0,2,4,6}$\n\nand so on. \n\nNotice that the only elements that lie in all the sets are $0$ and $2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{⋂}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}={0,2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071758/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b8d3481284f189b1c8e9a41b8d7e2aaa0114ab8d11d76052c51cb913db60674"} {"question" "q-174449" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071758/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "329b3f8b9e5ae2380f658ef1537c5a4febf7c7d1c95f0606f2882845984220fa"} {"question" "q-174449" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071758/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b8d3481284f189b1c8e9a41b8d7e2aaa0114ab8d11d76052c51cb913db60674"} {"question" "q-174449" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{0,1}"] ["math" "{0,2}"] ["math" "{1}"] ["math" "{2i}"] ["math" "∅"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071758/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b8d3481284f189b1c8e9a41b8d7e2aaa0114ab8d11d76052c51cb913db60674"} {"question" "q-174449" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{0,2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071758/state.json" "file_sha256" "6b8d3481284f189b1c8e9a41b8d7e2aaa0114ab8d11d76052c51cb913db60674"} {"question" "e-12665" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $T_2$ given that $T_n = \\{ 1, 2, \\ldots, 2n+1 \\},$ where $n \\in \\mathbb{N}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071758/example-12665.json" "file_sha256" "7c8f2fd4c9331d23223b9ed72c44cbe25944a0301ef200cd075a6e0a2036d29b"} {"question" "e-12665" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To write down the elements of $T_2,$ we substitute $n=2$ into the expression and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{2} & ={1,2,…,2(2)+1} \\\\  & ={1,2,…,5} \\\\  & ={1,2,3,4,5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071758/example-12665.json" "file_sha256" "7c8f2fd4c9331d23223b9ed72c44cbe25944a0301ef200cd075a6e0a2036d29b"} {"question" "e-12763" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $\\,\\displaystyle \\bigcup_{i \\in I} S_i$, given that $I = \\{ -1, 0, 1 \\},$ and $S_i = (i-1, \\,i+1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071758/example-12763.json" "file_sha256" "c174898ac48d7f2f07435fe3b30c9a7a668c3edf058dea5abbaa80d0fbf7b8ad"} {"question" "e-12763" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The union of a family of indexed sets is the set containing all elements belonging to *at least one* set in the indexed family:\n\n$$\n\\bigcup_{i \\in I} A_i = \\big\\{ x\\in U \\: : \\: x \\in A_i \\:\\:\\textrm{for at least one } A_i,\\:\\: i \\in I \\big\\}\n$$\n\nwhere $U$ is a universal set.\n\nTherefore, in our case, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{⋃}_{i\\in I}{S}_{i} & ={S}_{-1}\\cup {S}_{0}\\cup {S}_{1} \\\\  & =(-2,0)\\,\\cup \\,(-1,1)\\,\\cup \\,(0,2) \\\\  & =(-2,2).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071758/example-12763.json" "file_sha256" "c174898ac48d7f2f07435fe3b30c9a7a668c3edf058dea5abbaa80d0fbf7b8ad"} {"question" "e-12764" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $\\,\\displaystyle \\bigcap_{i \\in I} X_i$  given that $I = \\mathbb{N}$ and $X_i = \\{ i, \\, 2i \\}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071758/example-12764.json" "file_sha256" "d46137ff28d044e91a3ca320102ec59a127157340451299077f8c1db5138fa58"} {"question" "e-12764" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The intersection of a family of indexed sets $\\{A_i\\}_{i\\in I}$ contains all elements that belong to *all* sets in our family:\n\n$$\n\\bigcap_{i \\in I} A_i = \\big\\{ x\\in U \\: : \\: x \\in A_i \\:\\:\\textrm{for all } A_i,\\:\\: i \\in I \\big\\}\n$$\n\nwhere $U$ is a universal set.\n\nLet's now write down a few instances of our indexed sets:\n\n- if $i=1,$ we have $X_1 = \\{ 1, 2 \\}$\n\n- if $i=2,$ we have $X_2 = \\{ 2, 4 \\}$\n\n- if $i=3,$ we have $X_3 = \\{ 3, 6 \\}$\n\n- if $i=4,$ we have $X_4 = \\{ 4, 8 \\}$\n\nand so on. \n\nNotice that there is no element that belongs to all the sets. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{⋂}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}=∅.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071758/example-12764.json" "file_sha256" "d46137ff28d044e91a3ca320102ec59a127157340451299077f8c1db5138fa58"}] "usage" {"q-174340" [] "q-172662" [] "e-12763" [] "e-12665" [] "e-12764" [] "q-174432" [] "q-174350" [] "q-174447" [] "q-172665" []} "basis" 2583 "retractions" [[17592186054959 :question/problem "Let $A_{i} = {-i^{2}, 0, 2i}$, where $i ∈ {1, 2, 3, 4, 5}$. Then, $A_{2} =$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186051696 17592186051697 17592186051698 17592186051699 17592186051700 17592186051702 17592186051703 17592186051704 17592186051705 17592186051706 17592186301839 17592186301840 17592186301841 17592186301842 17592186301843 17592186301860 17592186301861 17592186301862 17592186301863 17592186301864 17592186301881 17592186301882 17592186301883 17592186301884 17592186301885 17592186301902 17592186301903 17592186301904 17592186301905 17592186301906] "immutable_fields" [[17592186051695 :answer-field/correct] [17592186051695 :answer-field/id] [17592186051695 :answer-field/key] [17592186051695 :answer-field/type] [17592186051701 :answer-field/correct] [17592186051701 :answer-field/id] [17592186051701 :answer-field/key] [17592186051701 :answer-field/type] [17592186301838 :answer-field/correct] [17592186301838 :answer-field/id] [17592186301838 :answer-field/key] [17592186301838 :answer-field/type] [17592186301859 :answer-field/correct] [17592186301859 :answer-field/id] [17592186301859 :answer-field/key] [17592186301859 :answer-field/type] [17592186301880 :answer-field/correct] [17592186301880 :answer-field/id] [17592186301880 :answer-field/key] [17592186301880 :answer-field/type] [17592186301901 :answer-field/correct] [17592186301901 :answer-field/id] [17592186301901 :answer-field/key] [17592186301901 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
